description:
Send one letter. Give to (an agent's name; daemon = its daemon folder, default yours) or box (a mailbox folder path, like the reply_to of a letter you read). status is one of REQUEST, DONE, BLOCKED, NEEDS-USER, FAILED, PROGRESS. title is one line that makes sense alone. what is the main text (for REQUEST: what the other agent should do and when it counts as done). outputs, not_done, decide are optional (default "none"). The answer comes back to your mailbox. Nothing is kept on your side unless you give keep (a file name in your workspace): then the sent letter is added to that file as one JSON line. Rules: when you finish a task someone asked for, send DONE, BLOCKED, NEEDS-USER or FAILED; if you are stuck for more than 10 minutes, send BLOCKED. Examples:
- ask bob: {"to": "bob", "status": "REQUEST", "title": "Please count the .csv files in data/", "what": "Count the .csv files in data/ and answer DONE with the number."}
- answer a letter you read: {"box": "/path/from/its/reply_to", "in_reply_to": "its letter name", "status": "DONE", "title": "data/ has 3 .csv files", "what": "I counted the .csv files in data/: 3.", "outputs": "none"}
- ask bob and keep a record: {"to": "bob", "status": "REQUEST", "title": "Please count the .csv files in data/", "what": "Count them and answer DONE with the number.", "keep": "mail/letters.jsonl"}
Errors: ArgumentsBad, StatusBad, WriteFailed, MailboxMissing, MailboxBad, InstanceMissing, DaemonMissing.
